# R6 allowlist — deliberately-unused parameters with a recorded rationale.
#
# R6 flags any engine function parameter named `_x` (TypeScript's marker for
# deliberately unused) because that shape has produced the same defect three
# times: regulatory citations dropped at verdict assembly, platform_satisfies
# never read, and safety_margin threaded and discarded (HR-14).
#
# An entry here is an EXCEPTION, not a fix. Each needs a rationale on the
# line above it, and each is fair game at review — that is the point. A gap
# with a written reason is an audit trail; a gap with no reason is the defect
# R6 exists to catch.
#
# Format: <file>:<function>:<parameter>

# Deliberate, recorded in P4-C03: the spec signature exposes only questionId,
# not which graph field each answer targeted, so answer-vs-answer
# contradiction is not derivable from it. Description-vs-graph contradiction
# is implemented; extending this needs a spec change, not a code change.
contradiction.ts:detectContradictions:_answers

# Unbuilt: pack-aware question narrowing. Questions should shrink when a
# jurisdiction rule already settles a dimension (the neighbour of PV-4).
# Note the caller in IntakeFlow.tsx passes a literal [] as well, so the
# feature is unimplemented at both ends. Removing the parameter would erase
# the seam; it is kept and recorded instead.
question-generator.ts:generateQuestions:_activePacks
